Data. Page 9. Tanda, 2011) and are veriﬁed by our data. The sorted values for/Delta1v10 show a heterogeneity in response to training. In comparison to the ﬁndings from Bouchard and Rankinen (2001), the portion of the population who showed a negative or no improvement in our investigation was higher. We believe that the higher portion was due to the unsupervised nature of the data as well as the low threshold of > 0.8 · hrmax we set to verify the best 10 km performances. However, increasing the threshold of hrmax to elevate the cardiopulmonary eﬀort for the best 10 km velocities did not change the proportion of training responses.

